The source is "3+2*2".
Keep a shared stack as an empty list of whole numbers.
Keep a shared number as 0.
Keep a shared lastcode as 0.
Set lastcode to 1.
Keep a shared depth as 0.
Keep a shared total as 0.
To multiply.
The top is item (depth minus 1) of stack.
remove the last item from stack.
Set depth to depth minus 1.
The product is top times number.
Place product into stack.
Add 1 to depth.
Set number to 0.

To divide.
The top is item (depth minus 1) of stack.
remove the last item from stack.
Set depth to depth minus 1.
The quotient is top divided by number.
Place quotient into stack.
Add 1 to depth.
Set number to 0.

To settle.
If lastcode is 1, Place number into stack, add 1 to depth, set number to 0.
If lastcode is 2, The neg is 0 minus number, Place neg into stack, add 1 to depth, set number to 0.
If lastcode is 3, multiply.
If lastcode is 4, divide.

The last is the last position of source.
For every spot from 0 to last.
The symbol is character spot of source.
If symbol is between "0" and "9", The digit is the digit value of symbol, set number to number times 10 plus digit.
If symbol is "+", settle, set lastcode to 1.
If symbol is "-", settle, set lastcode to 2.
If symbol is "*", settle, set lastcode to 3.
If symbol is "/", settle, set lastcode to 4.

Settle.
For each value in stack, add value to total.

Show total.
